# Anti-Over-Engineering (Auto)

Only change what was asked. Simplest solution first. When unsure, ask at Scout/Architect — do not invent scope.

## Do not
- Modify unrequested files or “drive-by” refactors — this tree has 270+ block folders under `src/`
- Add abstractions, helpers, or layers without a concrete need
- Install new npm/Composer packages that are not already in the project
- Rewrite entire files for small fixes
- Add error handling for impossible scenarios
- Expand a single-block task into a plugin-wide sweep, mass attribute rename, or bulk `block.json` migration
- Add ui-ux / motion skill packs or animation/design-system work beyond the approved task

## Sync-pipeline guard (project-specific)
- `src/` blocks are regenerated by `scripts/sync-src-from-mk.py` from `/Users/clickrmedia/mawkunn/twork-builder`
- Editing a synced block in `src/` is **thrown away on the next `npm run build` / `npm start`**
- Before editing a block: check `SKIP_BLOCKS` in `scripts/sync-src-from-mk.py`
  - In `SKIP_BLOCKS` → hand-written, safe to edit here
  - Not in `SKIP_BLOCKS` → edit upstream, or add it to `SKIP_BLOCKS` **only when the user approves**
- Never bulk-add blocks to `SKIP_BLOCKS` to make an edit “stick”

## Before delivery
- Diff scope matches the user request + approved `active_context.md`
- Prefer patching the existing block / `includes/*.php` / `assets/js` over new architecture
- Do not scaffold a new build system, TS migration, monorepo layout, or framework into this `wp-scripts` plugin
- Do not commit `build/`, `dist/`, or a new zip unless the task is a release
- If a simpler approach exists, use it
